{
  "chapter": "durability/scale-and-qos",
  "tier": "drill",
  "notes": [
    "Priority determines which sub-queue a task enters. Fairness determines dispatch",
    "order within each priority level. The two are not competing knobs.",
    "Priority runs 1 (highest) to 5 (lowest) and is strict: every 1 goes before any 4.",
    "Within a level, tenants take turns in order of first appearance, each taking as many",
    "tasks per round as its weight. A tenant with nothing left is skipped, not waited for.",
    "Weights are integers here; the chapter's 2.0 and 1.0 are 2 and 1. A tenant with no",
    "declared weight takes one turn."
  ],
  "weights": { "enterprise-a": 2, "standard-b": 1, "standard-c": 1 },
  "cases": [
    {
      "id": "one-tenant-at-one-priority-is-plain-fifo",
      "tasks": [
        { "id": "t1", "priority": 3, "tenant": "standard-b" },
        { "id": "t2", "priority": 3, "tenant": "standard-b" },
        { "id": "t3", "priority": 3, "tenant": "standard-b" }
      ],
      "result": ["t1", "t2", "t3"]
    },
    {
      "id": "live-chat-drains-before-the-normal-queue",
